docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-11.md:135:| 8 | `phase-0-prereg-amendment-10.md:443-447`, `:449-457`, `:462` (A10.4 option (e), A10.4.1); A10.7 rows 25–33 and 37–39 (`:761-769`, `:773-775`); the plain-language summary `:106-124`, the additions list `:213-226`, the row-26 note `:432`, the closing summary `:795-799` and the reconciliation item `:810-812` (c018, c103; A11X-02, A11XC-01) | option (e) AUTHOR ADOPTED with A10.4.1; the listing cut only "for schedule reasons" (`:455-456`); "rows 25–33 and 37–39 only on (e)" (`:446-447`) | (V1) option (e) is narrowed by the author's E9 row 2 ruling of 2026-10-23 (`docs/reviews/e9-packet/AUTHOR-RULINGS.md:5-12`). It is an author scope decision, not the schedule cut order. A10.4.1 and rows 25–32 and 37–39 do not apply to V1. The passages at `:106-124` ("Key substitution: option (e)", "the limits", "time"), `:213-226` (the listing's field, check, reason codes and invariants) and `:432` describe the listing as a V1 mechanism. They are kept as the dated record of the 2026-10-18 adoption, with the author's words, and are superseded as descriptions of V1: in V1 no verifier rejects a receipt for keys missing from a list, no listing pre-commitment or listing-evidence preservation duty exists, and after capture of both authority channels a receipt under the attacker's own keys passes (`docs/V1-CONTRACT.md` §2 after G10, §4). The closing summary's listing mechanisms and "option (e) deliberately rejects new cases: receipts under unlisted keys, and receipts whose listing was not pre-committed" (`:795-799`) are superseded for V1 in the same way, and the listing parts of the reconciliation item at `:810-812` (the listing-evidence package, the listing subchecks and their total-order rows, the C0/C1 bootstrap) are withdrawn as V1 work. Every other mention of A10.4.1 in A10 (the status block `:13-28`, the author's quotations `:273` and `:620`, the "no longer open" note `:805`, and the mechanism section `:462-611`, all of A10.4.1) is the dated record of the adoption or the mechanism text itself, superseded for V1 by this row. The frozen copies in `formal/freeze-v1/objects/spec.bin` are covered by the same disposition; their bytes are not edited. The owner grepped every registered and frozen text for the listing's vocabulary on 2026-10-29, and no other mention remains undisposed. Release-key custody (A10.4.2) is separate and unchanged. Option (a) applies (rows 15–16). A10.4.2 (rows 34–36) is unchanged. Row 33 stands as registered cut-order text, since (e) is narrowed, not withdrawn. Its "second item cut is the service-key listing" has no referent in V1. Its other sentences (option (a) applies, the absence of new-key protection is stated, no cure for release-key independence) are met by the ruling and profile §5 (`270ca49:docs/V1-PROFILE.md:619-623`). Profile :619-622 and :1258-1262 are then consistent as written. Kind C/W, recorded here because no signed change table lists it |
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-11.md:139:| 12 | **K-R.** `formal/p8/HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT.md:61-64`, `:152-153`, `:173-174`, `:524`, `:533`, `:274-276` (the supplement's copy of the E§5.2 replacement text); `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md:557-559` (c004, c008, c011, c097, c108; A11X-01) | :61 "it is the issuer's only path"; :63-64 "the issuer always computes `μ` … and sends `μ`"; :152-153 "Every issuer KMS `Sign` call on the key is `MessageType EXTERNAL_MU`, with `μ` computed by the issuer from such an `F`"; :173-174 "(K-R) is an issuer-code and IAM assumption: the key policy grants `kms:Sign` only to the issuer role, and the issuer code builds only V1 frames"; :524 "the issuer always uses EXTERNAL_MU for the kms slot, attestations and possession alike"; :533 "`kms:Sign` only for the issuer role"; ENC:557-558 and its copy at supplement :274-275 "The issuer obtains `S_kms` (attestation and possession) from KMS with `MessageType EXTERNAL_MU` only, sending μ" | In each sentence, the actor that computes `μ` and calls `kms:Sign` is the KMS-slot policy signer (`service/signer-kms/`). It runs in the issuing AWS account under its own IAM role. It computes `μ` only from an `F` it has validated: tag, alg, key fingerprint, ε (attestation frames only; manifests carry no declared time, HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT:495), `sign_by`, the signing stop (`service/signer-kms/tessera_sign_kms/signer.py:176-185`). Its role is the only `kms:Sign` principal, and the issuer roles hold no KMS permission (`service/signer-kms/infra/main.tf:33-34`; `service/issuer/infra/main.tf:181`). :173-174 reads: "(K-R) is a signer-code and IAM assumption: the key policy grants `kms:Sign` only to the KMS-slot policy signer's role, and that signer signs only V1 frames it has validated." **The (K-R) restrictions are unchanged** (:151-153, :157): the key signs only V1 tagged strings, in pure mode with the empty context, and is used by no other protocol or service. Only the actor that enforces them changes, so the wording of :152-153 changes as stated. The historical capture labels "selected issuer path" and "issuer-computed μ" (:76, :353, :412, :478) describe the 2026-10-13/14 captures and still fit (A11X-01, A11X-05). EXTERNAL_MU only, for attestations and possession alike, is unchanged. The verifier side is unchanged. Kind R |
