docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:23:| S4 latency | **Stated, not guaranteed:** a receipt is usually complete within 3 hours of acceptance. *(Revised 2026-10-29: the earlier "a request not complete 24 hours after acceptance ends as FAILED" contradicted the registered lifecycle, A2.1 and A2.3, and is withdrawn; Amendment 11 c016, `docs/decisions/2026-10-29-issuance-lifecycle.md`.)* A request makes up to three attempts. Each attempt can expire only after `declared + δ + S` (96 hours), and only on complete evidence that it was not timely. A request ends COMPLETE, or REFUSED (`ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED` or `SIGNING_CLOSED`) with each attempt's reason. N × (δ + S), twelve days, is a nominal budget, not a promise. Ending an attempt whose evidence stays unobtainable awaits an author decision; until then, such an attempt stays open. Start: the acceptance response. End: the status becoming COMPLETE or REFUSED. Window preparation happens before the window opens and does not count. Results are **retrieved by the client**, not pushed. | Owner |
docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:42:| L1 window dates and closure | Both window endpoints are fixed and published before issuance preparation, at most 90 days apart. The actual dates stay OPEN until the dated operating record; a late first issuance does not extend the window. Signing stops 96 hours before the window ends (the runbook's operating margin, not a registered rule). Acceptance stops at least δ + S + 24 hours (120 hours) before signing stops, that is at least 216 hours before the window ends, so that a first attempt always has its full lifecycle before signing stops. A later attempt that would need signing after the stop ends the request REFUSED `SIGNING_CLOSED`, which is a registered outcome; a closed signing window never ends a latched or already signed and stamped attempt. *(Revised 2026-10-29, Amendment 11 c016.)* Only receipts that pass the registered window checks are shipped. Completed results stay retrievable for 30 days (S5). Closure is announced 14 days ahead on the service page. | Owner |
